mapledmaaddr (#528) -- KILL TABLE 6 (TARGETED), PRETABLE, written 2026-09-12 BEFORE the table runs.  Post-table notes go
in a SEPARATE file (POSTTABLE.out).

WHY.  The closing pass on table 5's class closure (scriptable seats _scratchpad/panel_20260912_190504/, 7/7 produced
output -- codex's was REFUSED by its content filter, a seat failure to re-fire; the Opus measuring seat
../opus_close_20260912/OPUS_REPORT.md) found the TIME axis: deepseek, kimi (CLI and substitute) and glm predicted, and
Opus MEASURED 37/37, a read arm that registers an exit-time diagnostic (`atexit(maple_dmaaddr_atexit)', the handler
calling fatal()).  Table 5 read a snapshot taken BEFORE `quit' was typed, so everything after it was unobserved --
"the exemption wasn't removed; it was generalised from one line to an unbounded time window" (Opus).  AND IT IS A
REGRESSION THE REPAIR ITSELF INTRODUCED: table 4's grammar scanned the whole buffer, so the same diagnostic after
`quit' would have been an off-grammar line.  Table 5's PRETABLE called the new oracle "a strict tightening" of table
4's -- FALSE on the time axis (glm).  grok and minimax graded it outside the contract as written; the contract as
written was the defect, and Opus graded it a breach of the floor ("interval silence" means the read may not announce
itself, whenever the announcement lands).  Either way the repair costs one line of scope, so it is taken (L1).

THE CHANGE (noise() scope + the post-quit read; no row, no session changed; still 37 rows):
  * session() no longer snapshots; after typing `quit' it reads to the pty's EOF (rd(10.0) returns at once on EOF).
  * noise(t, cmds) compares the WHOLE transcript -- first prompt to EOF -- with owed(cmds + ["quit"]): `quit' owes
    exactly its echo, then the transcript must end (the only trailing element is the final newline's "").
  * Header: the silence sentence says "WHOLE transcript ... to the pty's EOF" and names late output; NOT COVERED adds
    output on a channel the pty never carries (a file, syslog).
MEASURED BEFORE THIS BLOCK: 37/37 CONTROL=OK on the fixed build/ binary (BASE_prelaunch.out, _scratchpad/
maple_base37b.out) -- a clean session prints nothing after `GXemul> quit', as Opus's non-equivalence capture also shows.

WHY TARGETED.  Against table 5's oracle the new one is a SUPERSET (and this time the claim is checked against the time
axis too): every table-5 red is a mismatch, a bad tail or a bare CR inside the pre-quit prefix of the transcript, and
that prefix is still compared line for line -- a bad pre-quit tail now shows up as a non-owed line before the `quit'
echo.  The new oracle adds only the post-quit suffix.  Value rows unchanged.  So: BASE three times (no false red --
the post-quit read to EOF is new code), HEAD, M_ATEXIT on BOTH instruments, and the channel's regression legs.

MUTATOR: mut_maple6.py = table 5's plus M_ATEXIT, two edits in one leg, VERBATIM from ../opus_close_20260912/
M_ATEXIT.diff (the +/- lines diffed against Opus's: identical).  The mutator now accepts a list of edits per leg.

PREDICTIONS -- FROZEN6 (the whole-transcript probe), score / 37:
  BASE / BASE2 / BASE3   37/37 CONTROL=OK
  HEAD            11/37  as table 5 (25 value rows + read silent)
  M_EXITONLY      11/37  as table 5
  M_ATEXIT        36/37  read silent alone, 12/12 sessions (every read session reads DMAADDR, so every one registers
                         the handler and prints `[ dreamcast_maple: DMAADDR was read ]' after `GXemul> quit')
  M_KEEPFATAL / M_HEXDIAG / M_BLANKDIAG / M_CRDIAG / M_PROMPTDIAG / M_GLUEPROMPT / M_QUITLINE   36/37, read silent alone
  M_ORBIT31       36/37  zero reread alone
  M_READCLEAR     33/37  width8, ones reread, double 2, reread 3
PREDICTIONS -- FROZEN5 (table 5's pre-quit-snapshot probe), score / 37:
  BASE            37/37
  M_ATEXIT        37/37  ESCAPE -- the Opus seat's measurement, reproduced in this table's own clone

CHECKS.  CLAIM -> ROW: the header's "a line printed late" -> read silent + M_ATEXIT.  CHANNEL: M_ATEXIT's observable is
